# {{.Module}}

A TableTheory (Python) quickstart scaffold generated by `tabletheory init --lang py`.

## What's here

- `main.py` — a create/read/delete program using TableTheory against DynamoDB Local.
- `dms.yml` — the language-neutral DMS description of the `Note` model.
- `docker-compose.yml` — DynamoDB Local (no AWS account required).

## Run it (one command)

```bash
python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
docker compose up -d
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=dummy AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=dummy AWS_REGION=us-east-1 \
  DYNAMODB_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000 python main.py
```

Expected final line:

```
OK: TableTheory CRUD against DynamoDB Local succeeded
```

## Installing the runtime

TableTheory is distributed through GitHub Releases (not PyPI). `requirements.txt` pins
the release wheel. Update the URL to a different release with the version you want; the
canonical import package is `tabletheory_py` (the legacy `theorydb_py` import also works).

## Next steps

- Edit `dms.yml`, then regenerate a matching Python model with `tabletheory gen --lang py dms.yml`.
- Generate CDK table constructs with `tabletheory gen --cdk dms.yml`.
- Point at real AWS by unsetting `DYNAMODB_ENDPOINT` and providing AWS credentials.
